 #include <string>
 
 // Checks GitHub for a newer release and installs it over the program's own files. The check runs once, on a
-// thread of its own, and only reads the latest release's tag. An install downloads the release's zip, then a
-// script waits for the game to close and copies the zip's files over the game's folder, leaving the player's
-// own folders (data, game) alone. Windows only; elsewhere nothing is ever reported as available.
+// thread of its own, and only reads the latest release's tag. An install downloads the release's package (a .zip on
+// Windows; a .tar.gz with "linux" or "macos" in its name elsewhere, fetched with curl), has a hidden script unpack it
+// beside the game while the game runs, and once the game has closed the script puts the files over the game's folder,
+// leaving the player's own folders (data, game) alone, and starts the game again. Not on Android.
 namespace portablekit::ui::updater {
 
 enum class State { Idle, Checking, UpToDate, Available, Failed, Downloading, Unpacking, Ready };
